Subject: [PATCH] rp2350: fix the malformed ARCH_RP2350 Kconfig block

Patch 0011 nested 'config GOLDFISH', 'config IRQ_STACKS' and the help text
inside the ARCH_RP2350 entry.  'config' is a keyword, not an attribute, so those
lines actually terminated ARCH_RP2350 and started two new symbols, leaving
ARCH_RP2350 with no help text and attaching the RP2350 help to IRQ_STACKS.

Give ARCH_RP2350 its own help text and drop the nested redefinitions.  GOLDFISH
is already pinned to n in the board fragment; IRQ_STACKS is pinned there too
now, preserving the previous .config exactly.

---
--- a/arch/riscv/Kconfig.socs	2026-11-07 15:50:22.446950109 +0800
+++ b/arch/riscv/Kconfig.socs	2026-11-07 15:55:32.320420854 +0800
@@ -30,12 +30,9 @@
 	select MTD_PHRAM
 	select CRAMFS
 	select CRAMFS_MTD
-	config GOLDFISH
-		def_bool n
-	config IRQ_STACKS
-		def_bool n
 	help
-          This enables support for Raspberry Pi RP2350 microcontroller.
+	  This enables support for the Raspberry Pi RP2350 microcontroller
+	  (Hazard3 RISC-V core, nommu, QSPI flash + PSRAM).
 
 config ARCH_SIFIVE
 	bool "SiFive SoCs"
